Bound every read of font data to the file.

stb_truetype.h opens with "NO SECURITY GUARANTEE -- DO NOT USE THIS ON UNTRUSTED FONT FILES" and
reads wherever the table offsets in the file point; the CFF reader even sizes its buffer as 512 MB.
Reader fonts come off the SD card and from the network font installer, and test/fuzz/ttf crashed
this build within seconds of starting, so the reads are checked:

  - ttBYTE/ttCHAR/ttUSHORT/ttSHORT/ttULONG/ttLONG return 0 outside [stbtt__lo, stbtt__hi). The
    window is set by the new stbtt_BindData() for the whole file and re-set from the fontinfo
    (data, data_end) at every entry point that takes one.
  - the CFF buffer ends at the end of the file instead of 512 MB past its table.
  - the glyph point stream of a simple glyph cannot run past the end of the file, and the
    vertices written cannot outgrow the m allocated (contour ends in a hostile glyph need not
    ascend).
  - composite glyphs nest at most 4 deep and draw at most 64 components per glyph, so a glyph
    that names itself, or fans out in every level, ends instead of recursing or looping.

The window is one pair of globals: stb must be called from one task at a time, as the render path
already does.

